· A simulation‑based validation using a digital twin in NVIDIA Isaac Sim, complemented by separate computational models for washing hygiene, peeling forces, and cutting accuracy (Chapter 5). The study predicts that the SPS can achieve a preparation time reduction of ∼2.4×, peel waste below 7 %, and cut uniformity within ±0.5 mm.
· A thorough discussion of the technical risks, regulatory pathway, intellectual property landscape, and commercialisation strategy, together with a concrete roadmap for future prototyping and experimental validation (Chapter 6).

