Appendix E: Pseudocode for Key Algorithms

E.1 Perception Pipeline (ROS 2 node)

```
function perception_loop():
    while true:
        rgb, depth = get_camera_frame()
        masks, classes = efficientdet_inference(rgb)  // quantized INT8
        point_cloud = depth_to_pointcloud(depth, rgb)
        for each instance i:
            hull = convex_hull(point_cloud[masks[i]])
            volume = hull.volume()
            mass_raw = load_cell_reading()
            state[i] = ekf_update(classes[i], volume, mass_raw)
            if nir_enabled:
                spectrum = nir_spectrometer.read()
                maturity[i] = maturity_regression(rgb_histogram(rgb[masks[i]]), spectrum)
            else:
                maturity[i] = maturity_regression_rgb_only(rgb_histogram(rgb[masks[i]]))
        publish_state_estimate(state)
        sleep(100 ms)
```

E.2 Batch Scheduler (MILP)

```
function schedule_batch(items):
    // items: list of (type, target_cut, state_estimate)
    // Build MILP model
    model = create_milp()
    for each item i:
        p_i = lookup_preptime(item)
        add_processing_time_variable(i, p_i)
    for each pair (i, j):
        s_ij = tool_change_time(item[i].cut, item[j].cut)
        add_setup_time_constraint(i, j, s_ij)
    objective = minimize(makespan + lambda * sum(tool_changes))
    solve(model)  // using OR‑Tools, timeout 100 ms
    return optimal_sequence
```

E.3 MPC Controller for Single Ingredient

```
function mpc_control(ingredient_state, user_weights):
    // ingredient_state = (type, volume, mass, maturity)
    u_opt = lookup_table[type][quantize(ingredient_state)][user_weights]
    // u_opt contains: t_wash, tau_peel_profile, g_cut, v_blade
    if uncertainty(ingredient_state) > threshold:
        // adopt conservative policy (thicker peel, slower cut)
        u_opt = adjust_for_uncertainty(u_opt)
    return u_opt
```

