Appendix I: Foreign Object Detection Model Design

I.1 Network Architecture

A MobileNetV3‑Small backbone with an SSD detection head, retrained to detect three classes: stone, metal fragment, large seed. Input resolution: 320×320 px. Run on the safety MCU with a dedicated INT8 inference engine (TensorFlow Lite Micro). The model is lightweight: < 1 M parameters, < 100 ms inference time.

I.2 Training Data Plan

· Synthetic data: 50 000 images generated by pasting foreign object cutouts onto clean vegetable backgrounds (from real kitchen photos) with realistic lighting, wetness, and occlusion.
· Real validation set: 500 images of actual foreign objects placed in a mock‑up drawer, manually labelled. This set will be used to measure the sim‑to‑real gap and fine‑tune the model.

I.3 Performance Targets

· Detection rate (true positive) > 95 % for objects larger than 5 mm in any dimension.
· False positive rate on normal produce < 1 %.
· Safety action: if confidence > 95 %, abort cycle and alert user.

Current status: Model designed but not yet trained or validated. Real‑world testing is essential before certifying as a safety function.

